er myself. Window: 2026-08-01 to 2026-12-31. That could be many events but fine.\n\nLet me call listEvents with timeMin 2026-08-01T00:00:00Z, timeMax 2026-12-31T23:59:59Z, max 250. Then I can identify rebrand-related.\n\nActually, let me use query \"rebrand\" to be targeted, and also consider. But I''ll do a full list to be comprehensive since calendars are small. Let me do full list.\n\nI''ll call listEvents once. Then filter for rebrand-related.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"listEvents is loaded (available next turn). I''ll call it with a wide window covering the rebrand timeframe. Since \"rebrand\" events span Sept-Oct 2026, let me use a window from Sep 1 2026 to Nov 30 2026, with query \"rebrand\". Actually query might filter by title. Let me use query \"rebrand\" and a broad window.\n\nActually, better to list events with query \"rebrand\" over a wide window. But the events might be titled \"Aozora logo review\" etc. — \"Aozora\" is the rebrand client? The rebrand review invitation from Raj was explicitly \"Rebrand review\". Let me query \"rebrand\" first. But to be thorough about \"related to the rebrand,\" I might also include Aozora. Hmm.\n\nThe user asked \"anything in my calendar related to the rebrand?\" The obvious one is \"Rebrand review\". But there might be others. Let me list with a broad window and query \"rebrand\". If the query matches only title, I might miss Aozora ones. Let me do a broad listing without query to see all events in the window, then filter myself. Window: 2026-08-01 to 2026-12-31. That could be many events but fine.\n\nLet me call listEvents with timeMin 2026-08-01T00:00:00Z, timeMax 2026-12-31T23:59:59Z, max 250. Then I can identify rebrand-related.\n\nActually, let me use query \"rebrand\" to be targeted, and also consider. But I''ll do a full list to be comprehensive since calendars are small. Let me do full list.\n\nI''ll call listEvents once. Then filter for rebrand-related."}],"createdAt":1793759307743},{"type":"tool-in