uld check the remaining subfolders: Team/website, Team/Offsite 2026, Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand, Clients/Saffron & Sage has no subfolder... and Finance/2025 done. Let me do a few more to be safe: Aozora Rebrand across 7? that''s heavy. Let''s do on two representative drives (SFTP A and S3 G) — actually the point is whether drives differ from each other, so comparing two is enough plus structural.\n\nActually a better completeness move: check Team/website, Team/Offsite 2026, Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand on drive A and G, plus check whether any subfolder differs across the 4 FTP/SFTP/S3... Hmm. Given clear mirroring so far, I''ll check the remaining subfolders on two drives plus one more FTP to confirm; but risk of overdoing.\n\nI think reasonable: verify the remaining three subfolders on drive A (SFTP) and G (S3) — 6 calls. If identical names/sizes, conclude mirrored.\n\nLet me do that.\n\nActually also worth noting sizes may match but content could differ — could read a text file from two drives to compare. E.g., read \"Team/Meeting notes 2026-10-05.md\" from drive A and G and compare. And welcome.txt. That''s a good content check. I need a read-file tool. Search for it.\n\nLet me do: search_tools for \"read file text\", and in parallel list remaining subfolders.\n\nI can''t call search_tools results in the same turn... it says tools become available next turn. So search now, and list folders now.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything matches in names and sizes. The only differences:\n1. Two S3 drives (b4199497, 1ae0b7b1) carry an extra top-level `edge/` folder — 15 entries of test fixtures (deep, unicode, mislabeled, bulk-2500, etc.).\n2. Scoped FTP drive (766b212a) only exposes `Clients/` — no Finance/, Team/, welcome.txt, and no edge/.\n3. Metadata differences: modifiedAt present on SFTP/WebDAV/S3 file listing but null on FTP drives; mimeType reported on SFTP/FTP/WebDAV but null on S3.\n\nCaveat: I compared the structure and file names/sizes at ro