93759511391,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Now do a content spot-check: read brief.md from drive A and G, and welcome.txt from A and G. getFileText is now loaded.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Now do a content spot-check: read brief.md from drive A and G, and welcome.txt from A and G. getFileText is now loaded."}],"createdAt":1793759518071},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"fileId":"Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand/brief.md","name":"brief.md","truncated":false,"text":"# Aozora Ceramics rebrand\n\nPrepared for Fernhill Studio by Kenji Watanabe, brand manager at Aozora Ceramics.\n\n## Audience\n\nDesign-led cafes, restaurants and home cooks in Japan and Europe.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- Wordmark and mark, three options at the first review\n- Colour and type system\n- Packaging for mugs, plates and the gift box\n\n## Timeline\n\n| Milestone | Date |\n| --- | --- |\n| Kickoff | 2026-10-05 |\n| First review | 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC |\n| Final files | 2026-11-20 |\n\n> Keep the colour blue somewhere. It has been on every Aozora cup since 1962.\n\nBudget: JPY 1,850,000, agreed in the signed proposal.\n"},"toolCallId":"call-247c7f5b-98fe-4c0a-94ef-7d46dff07f94","toolName":"getFileText","args":{"driveId":"36600459-5ed5-55e6-8cb3-f158ce3b8910","fileId":"Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand/brief.md"}},"updatedAt":1793759518903},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"fileId":"Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand/brief.md","name":"brief.md","truncated":false,"text":"# Aozora Ceramics rebrand\n\nPrepared for Fernhill Studio by Kenji Watanabe, brand manager at Aozora Ceramics.\n\n## Audience\n\nDesign-led cafes, restaurants and home cooks in Japan and Europe.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- Wordmark and mark, three options at the first review\n- Colour and type system\n- Packaging for mugs, plates and the gift box\n\n## Timeline\n\n| Milestone | Date |\n| --- | --- |\n| Kickoff | 2026-10-05 |\n| First review | 2026-10-08 15:00 UTC |\n| Final files | 2026-11-20 |\n\n> Keep the colour blue somewhere. It has been on every Aozora cup since 1962.\n\nBudget: JPY 1,850,000, agreed in the signed proposal.\n"},"toolCallId":"call-14df69d2-62e5-45e7-9460-7f6c86a037d7","toolName":"getFileText","args":{"driveId":"1ae0b7b1-7ad0-5805-82b9-169bd8978c60","fileId":"Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand/brief.md"}},"updatedAt":1793759518905},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"fileId":"welcome.txt","name":"welcome.txt","truncated":false,"text":"Welcome to the Fernhill Studio shared drive.\n\nClient work lives under Clients/, invoices and budgets under Finance/, and everything else under Team/.\nAsk Sam for access to Finance/.\n"},"toolCallId":"call-9f39c51c-01eb-468d-bbfa-2e069954a3a0","toolName":"getFileText","args":{"driveId":"36600459-5ed5-55e6-8cb3-f158ce3b8910","fileId":"welcome.txt"}},"updatedAt":1793759518906},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"fileId":"welcome.txt","name":"welcome.txt","truncated":false,"text":"Welcome to the Fernhill Studio shared drive.\n\nClient work lives under Clients/, invoices and budgets under Finance/, and everything else under Team/.\nAsk Sam for access to Finance/.\n"},"toolCallId":"call-1b50ece5-5bf6-4594-8974-6fc3698aca53","toolName":"getFileText","args":{"driveId":"1ae0b7b1-7ad0-5805-82b9-169bd8978c60","fileId":"welcome.txt"}},"updatedAt":1793759518908},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793759518912,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Conclusion: The 6 unscoped drives are mirror copies of the same Fernhill Studio shared drive — identical tree, names, sizes, and byte-identical text content. Differences:\n\n1. Two S3 drives (b4199497, 1ae0b7b1) have an extra top-level `edge/` folder with 15 entries — test fixtures (big, bulk-2500, case, deep, docs, empty-folder, folder-marker, images, mislabeled, preview, special, unicode, plus empty.txt, no-content-type.bin, one-byte). These two appear to be the same as each other.\n2. FTP #3 (766b212a) is scoped: only `Clients/` visible — 3 client folders, same contents. No Finance/, Team/, welcome.txt.\n3. Metadata gaps: the 3 FTP drives return null modifiedAt (all of them) — and S3 returns null mimeType for files. So listing metadata differs even where content is the same.\n\nAlso note two of the FTP drives (d4dacf11, 42ffd478) look identical to each other and to SFTP/WebDAV.\n\nAnswer with a table.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Conclusion: The 6 unscoped drives are mirror copies of the same Fernhill Studio shared drive — identical tree, names, sizes, and byte-identical text content. Differences:\n\n1. Two S3 drives (b4199497, 1ae0b7b1) have an extra top-level `edge/` folder with 15 entries — test fixtures (big, bulk-2500, case, deep, docs, empty-folder, folder-marker, images, mislabeled, preview, special, unicode, plus empty.txt, no-content-type.bin, one-byte). These two appear to be the same as each other.\n2. FTP #3 (766b212a) is scoped: only `Clients/` visible — 3 client folders, same contents. No Finance/, Team/, welcome.txt.\n3. Metadata gaps: the 3 FTP drives return null modifiedAt (all of them) — and S3 returns null mimeType for files. So listing metadata differs even where content is the same.\n\nAlso note two of the FTP drives (d4dacf11, 42ffd478) look identical to each other and to SFTP/WebDAV.\n\nAnswer with a table."}],"createdAt":1793759539209},{"type":"text","text":"**No — they''re near-identical mirrors of one \"Fernhill Studio\" shared drive, but not byte-for-byte identical.** Same tree, same file names, same sizes, and spot-checked text files are character-for-character the same. The differences are in what each endpoint exposes and what metadata it reports.\n\n**Structure (all 6 full drives):** `Clients/`, `Finance/2025/`, `Team/`, `welcome.txt` — matching at every level I checked:\n\n| Path | Contents (identical across drives) |\n|---|---|\n| `Clients/` | Aozora Ceramics, Kaltwasser GmbH, Saffron & Sage |\n| `Clients/Aozora Ceramics/` | `Proposal - signed.pdf` (789 B) + `Rebrand/` (brief.md, wordmark.svg, logo-options.png, moodboard.pdf, logo-pack.zip) |\n| `Clients/Saffron & Sage/` | `menu-proof.indd`, `musakhan.jpg`, `شعار.svg` |\n| `Clients/Kaltwasser GmbH/` | `Angebot 2026.docx`, `Pitch deck.pptx`, `Notizen Kickoff.md` |\n| `Finance/2025/` | `Budget 2025.xlsx`, `invoices.csv`, `expenses.tsv` |\n| `Team/` | `website/`, `Offsite 2026/`, `Meeting notes 2026-10-05.md`, `brand-tokens.json`, `voice-memo.wav`, `新しいロゴ案.png` |\n| `welcome.txt` | 182 B |\n\nContent check: `welcome.txt` and `Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand/brief.md` read back identically from the SFTP drive and an S3 drive.\n\n**The three real differences:**\n\n1. **The two S3 drives have an extra top-level `edge/` folder** that none of the others have — 15 entries of test fixtures (`big`, `bulk-2500`, `case`, `deep`, `docs`, `empty-folder`, `folder-marker`, `images`, `mislabeled`, `preview`, `special`, `unicode`, `empty.txt`, `one-byte`, `no-content-type.bin`). The two S3 drives match each other exactly.\n\n2. **FTP #3 (`766b212a…`) is scoped** — it only exposes `Clients/` (all three client folders, identical contents). No `Finance/`, no `Team/`, no `welcome.txt`, no `edge/`. That''s the folder grant, not missing data.\n\n3. **Metadata is uneven**, so a naive diff will show false mismatches: the three FTP drives return `modifiedAt: null` for every entry, and both S3 drives return `mimeType: null` for files. SFTP and WebDAV report full metadata (`modifiedAt 2026-11-03T17:20:56Z`).\n\n**So:** drives 1, 2, 4, 5 are indistinguishable copies; drives 6 and 7 are those same copies plus the `edge/` test set; drive 3 is a folder-scoped view of just `Clients/`.\n\nOne caveat: I compared the full tree down to every leaf folder and spot-checked contents, but I didn''t hash the binaries (`.pptx`, `.indd`, `.zip`, images). Sizes all match, which makes divergence unlikely. If you want certainty, I can read a couple of the text-based ones (`.csv`, `.tsv`, `.json`, `Dockerfile`) from each drive and diff them exactly.","createdAt":1793759539209}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**No — they''re near-identical mirrors of one \"Fernhill Studio\" shared drive, but not byte-for-byte identical.** Same tree, same file names, same sizes, and spot-checked text files are character-for-character the same. The differences are in what each endpoint exposes and what metadata it reports.\n\n**Structure (all 6 full drives):** `Clients/`, `Finance/2025/`, `Team/`, `welcome.txt` — matching at every level I checked:\n\n| Path | Contents (identical across drives) |\n|---|---|\n| `Clients/` | Aozora Ceramics, Kaltwasser GmbH, Saffron & Sage |\n| `Clients/Aozora Ceramics/` | `Proposal - signed.pdf` (789 B) + `Rebrand/` (brief.md, wordmark.svg, logo-options.png, moodboard.pdf, logo-pack.zip) |\n| `Clients/Saffron & Sage/` | `menu-proof.indd`, `musakhan.jpg`, `شعار.svg` |\n| `Clients/Kaltwasser GmbH/` | `Angebot 2026.docx`, `Pitch deck.pptx`, `Notizen Kickoff.md` |\n| `Finance/2025/` | `Budget 2025.xlsx`, `invoices.csv`, `expenses.tsv` |\n| `Team/` | `website/`, `Offsite 2026/`, `Meeting notes 2026-10-05.md`, `brand-tokens.json`, `voice-memo.wav`, `新しいロゴ案.png` |\n| `welcome.txt` | 182 B |\n\nContent check: `welcome.txt` and `Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand/brief.md` read back identically from the SFTP drive and an S3 drive.\n\n**The three real differences:**\n\n1. **The two S3 drives have an extra top-level `edge/` folder** that none of the others have — 15 entries of test fixtures (`big`, `bulk-2500`, `case`, `deep`, `docs`, `empty-folder`, `folder-marker`, `images`, `mislabeled`, `preview`, `special`, `unicode`, `empty.txt`, `one-byte`, `no-content-type.bin`). The two S3 drives match each other exactly.\n\n2. **FTP #3 (`766b212a…`) is scoped** — it only exposes `Clients/` (all three client folders, identical contents). No `Finance/`, no `Team/`, no `welcome.txt`, no `edge/`. That''s the folder grant, not missing data.\n\n3. **Metadata is uneven**, so a naive diff will show false mismatches: the three FTP drives return `modifiedAt: null` for every entry, and both S3 drives return `mimeType: null` for files. SFTP and WebDAV report full metadata (`modifiedAt 2026-11-03T17:20:56Z`).\n\n**So:** drives 1, 2, 4, 5 are indistinguishable copies; drives 6 and 7 are those same copies plus the `edge/` test set; drive 3 is a folder-scoped view of just `Clients/`.\n\nOne caveat: I compared the full tree down to every leaf folder and spot-checked contents, but I didn''t hash the binaries (`.pptx`, `.indd`, `.zip`, images). Sizes all match, which makes divergence unlikely. If you want certainty, I can read a couple of the text-based ones (`.csv`, `.tsv`, `.json`, `Dockerfile`) from each drive and diff them exactly."}','assistant','v2','2026-11-04T02:30:23.546Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
