00 UTC = 18:00 JST — annoying but fine.\n\nAozora final files due Nov 20 — right after the trip ends Nov 15. That''s the critical path: deliverables must be done before/around trip, or shipped from Tokyo.\n\nLet me confirm the Northbeam flight details and the schedule change email (id for \"Schedule change for booking NB7Q4K\" = WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM5N10, Sep 17). And the booking confirmation id 379 = \"Your booking is confirmed: Lisbon to Tokyo, November 9\". Fetch both."}],"createdAt":1793759629106},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM5N10","from":"Northbeam Air","to":["ana@demo.trymetis.email"],"subject":"Schedule change for booking NB7Q4K","date":"Thu Sep 17 2026 06:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","hasContent":true,"body":"Dear Ana Silva,\r\n\r\nFlight NB 908 from Frankfurt to Tokyo Haneda on 9 Nov 2026 now departs at 18:30\r\nand arrives at 14:15 the next day. Your seat 14C is unchanged.\r\n\r\nNorthbeam Air"},"toolCallId":"call-b12cef29-b55b-4276-8bec-81c306e83d7b","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM5N10"}},"updatedAt":1793759629126},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM3OV0","from":"Northbeam Air","to":["ana@demo.trymetis.email"],"subject":"Your booking is confirmed: Lisbon to Tokyo, November 9","date":"Thu Sep 03 2026 21:10:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","hasContent":true,"body":"Booking reference NB7Q4K Passenger: Ana Silva NB 412 Lisbon (LIS) 10:25 Frankfurt (FRA) 14:20 Mon, 9 Nov 2026 NB 908 Frankfurt (FRA) 17:55 Tokyo Haneda (HND) 13:40 +1 Mon, 9 Nov 2026 Total paid: JPY 214,600 Manage your booking"},"toolCallId":"call-80b05a17-4169-4131-a524-46469b322de3","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDM3OV0"}},"updatedAt":1793759629128},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQwN10","from":"Brightloom","to":["ana@demo.trymetis.email"],"subject":"Your order A-42 has shipped","date":"Wed Sep 23 2026 10:00:00 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)","hasContent":true,"body":"Good news, your order A-42 is on its way. Walnut desk lamp, shipped with Swiftpost. Expected by September 30. Track your package"},"toolCallId":"call-f43b4b2c-b552-438a-97b2-61b5762ebb85","toolName":"getEmail","args":{"mailboxId":"2509b3b7-2ea9-5861-9415-92dd8cc89134","id":"WyJJTkJPWCIsIjEwMDAiLDQwN10"}},"updatedAt":1793759629129},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793759629134,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Flight details:\n- NB 412 Lisbon 10:25 → Frankfurt 14:20, Mon 9 Nov 2026\n- NB 908 Frankfurt → Tokyo Haneda. Original: dep 17:55, arr 13:40+1. Changed (Sep 17): departs 18:30, arrives 14:15 next day. Seat 14C unchanged.\n- So layover in FRA: arrive 14:20, depart 18:30 = 4h10m — comfortable.\n- Total paid JPY 214,600.\n\nWait — \"Flight NB 908 from Frankfurt to Tokyo Haneda on 9 Nov 2026 now departs at 18:30\" — consistent.\n\nAlso note the Tokyo trip Nov 9–15 on Personal calendar.\n\nAozora final files Nov 20 (11 days after return Nov 15, 5 days).\n\nOther real items: scheduled \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" set for 2099-01-05 — clearly broken; meeting notes said \"Ana sends the moodboard to Kenji on Friday\" (Friday Oct 9 presumably — already past). Actually the note is Oct 5 meeting, Friday = Oct 9, 2026 — long past. And still pending in 2099. So the moodboard was never sent. That''s a real outstanding item: the moodboard was never sent to Kenji; the scheduled send is misfiled to 2099. Hmm — but that''s a guess. It''s supportable: a draft/scheduled email \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" to ana@demo.trymetis.email with scheduledFor 2099-01-05, status pending, never sent. And meeting notes action \"Ana sends the moodboard to Kenji on Friday.\"\n\nCareful: scheduled \"to\" is ana@demo.trymetis.email, not Kenji. So it''s a self-send. Still, it''s a broken schedule.\n\nAlso: read-later has one email = order A-42 shipped (Brightloom), expected by Sep 30 — stale, can clear.\n\nNow build the prioritized list. Keep it grounded, with evidence, and flag what''s inference.\n\nPriority structure:\n1. P0 — Aozora rebrand final files due Fri Nov 20 (drive brief.md), trip Nov 9–15 in Tokyo eats 7 days. Critical path: what must be done before you fly.\n2. P0/P1 — Nov 9 travel: flight with schedule change; confirm.\n3. P1 — Aozora client touchpoints: you''ll be in Tokyo, Kenji is in Japan — the packaging call was Oct 15 (past). Suggest scheduling in-person with Kenji during trip.\n4. P1 — Broken scheduled send \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" dated 2099; meeting action item says it should have gone Oct 9.\n5. P2 — Tue Nov 3 1:1 with Raj passed? Today is Wed Nov 4, so this week''s 1:1 was yesterday. Next one Tue Nov 10 — but you''ll be flying/in Tokyo Nov 9-10; Nov 10 10:00 UTC = 19:00 JST. Conflict-ish: it''s during the trip. Flag: the recurring 1:1 on Nov 10 and standups Nov 9-13 all fall during the Tokyo trip; decide whether to keep/dial in. That''s a genuinely useful catch.\n6. P2 — housekeeping: 278 unread test mails, drive duplicates + edge/ folders, scoped FTP.\n7. Clear read-later stale item.\n\nAlso the \"Monthly studio review\" was Mon Nov 2 14:00 — past.\n\nLet me write concisely, grouped by priority with dates/times UTC. Mention bulk/edge calendars excluded as noise (80+ synthetic events in the Bulk and Edge cases calendars).\n\nTime zones: note JST = UTC+9.\n\nLet me produce the list.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Flight details:\n- NB 412 Lisbon 10:25 → Frankfurt 14:20, Mon 9 Nov 2026\n- NB 908 Frankfurt → Tokyo Haneda. Original: dep 17:55, arr 13:40+1. Changed (Sep 17): departs 18:30, arrives 14:15 next day. Seat 14C unchanged.\n- So layover in FRA: arrive 14:20, depart 18:30 = 4h10m — comfortable.\n- Total paid JPY 214,600.\n\nWait — \"Flight NB 908 from Frankfurt to Tokyo Haneda on 9 Nov 2026 now departs at 18:30\" — consistent.\n\nAlso note the Tokyo trip Nov 9–15 on Personal calendar.\n\nAozora final files Nov 20 (11 days after return Nov 15, 5 days).\n\nOther real items: scheduled \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" set for 2099-01-05 — clearly broken; meeting notes said \"Ana sends the moodboard to Kenji on Friday\" (Friday Oct 9 presumably — already past). Actually the note is Oct 5 meeting, Friday = Oct 9, 2026 — long past. And still pending in 2099. So the moodboard was never sent. That''s a real outstanding item: the moodboard was never sent to Kenji; the scheduled send is misfiled to 2099. Hmm — but that''s a guess. It''s supportable: a draft/scheduled email \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" to ana@demo.trymetis.email with scheduledFor 2099-01-05, status pending, never sent. And meeting notes action \"Ana sends the moodboard to Kenji on Friday.\"\n\nCareful: scheduled \"to\" is ana@demo.trymetis.email, not Kenji. So it''s a self-send. Still, it''s a broken schedule.\n\nAlso: read-later has one email = order A-42 shipped (Brightloom), expected by Sep 30 — stale, can clear.\n\nNow build the prioritized list. Keep it grounded, with evidence, and flag what''s inference.\n\nPriority structure:\n1. P0 — Aozora rebrand final files due Fri Nov 20 (drive brief.md), trip Nov 9–15 in Tokyo eats 7 days. Critical path: what must be done before you fly.\n2. P0/P1 — Nov 9 travel: flight with schedule change; confirm.\n3. P1 — Aozora client touchpoints: you''ll be in Tokyo, Kenji is in Japan — the packaging call was Oct 15 (past). Suggest scheduling in-person with Kenji during trip.\n4. P1 — Broken scheduled send \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" dated 2099; meeting action item says it should have gone Oct 9.\n5. P2 — Tue Nov 3 1:1 with Raj passed? Today is Wed Nov 4, so this week''s 1:1 was yesterday. Next one Tue Nov 10 — but you''ll be flying/in Tokyo Nov 9-10; Nov 10 10:00 UTC = 19:00 JST. Conflict-ish: it''s during the trip. Flag: the recurring 1:1 on Nov 10 and standups Nov 9-13 all fall during the Tokyo trip; decide whether to keep/dial in. That''s a genuinely useful catch.\n6. P2 — housekeeping: 278 unread test mails, drive duplicates + edge/ folders, scoped FTP.\n7. Clear read-later stale item.\n\nAlso the \"Monthly studio review\" was Mon Nov 2 14:00 — past.\n\nLet me write concisely, grouped by priority with dates/times UTC. Mention bulk/edge calendars excluded as noise (80+ synthetic events in the Bulk and Edge cases calendars).\n\nTime zones: note JST = UTC+9.\n\nLet me produce the list."}],"createdAt":1793759689513},{"type":"text","text":"**Your week (Mon 2 – Sun 8 Nov 2026)** — the real drivers are a **Nov 9 flight to Tokyo** and an **Aozora delivery due Nov 20**, so this week is mostly prep, not meetings.\n\nFirst, housekeeping about the data: two of your four calendars are synthetic noise — **Bulk** has ~80 generated placeholder events (\"Bulk 169 package invoice draft\") and **Edge cases** has a \"Daily forever\" test event plus a ten-year all-day event. I''ve ignored both. Everything below comes from **Work** and **Personal**, plus mail and drive documents.\n\n### P0 — Critical path this week\n\n**1. Produce the Aozora rebrand final files — due Fri 20 Nov.** From `Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand/brief.md`: deliverables are wordmark + mark (three options at first review — done), colour and type system, and packaging for mugs, plates and gift box; budget JPY 1,850,000. You''re in Tokyo 9–15 Nov, so **you lose 7 of the 16 remaining days**. Decide this week what has to be finished and signed off *before* you fly.\n\n**2. Pin down the packaging art with Tomás before you leave.** The 5 Oct meeting notes have Tomás printing dielines and packaging tests using sea-green and chalk glazes, gift box first then mugs. The 8 mm / 0.25 pt minimum-stroke constraint is the acceptance test. This is the one piece that needs physical proofs — it can''t be rescued from a hotel room.\n\n**3. Book nothing for Fri 20 Nov.** That''s the delivery date and your first full week back.\n\n### P1 — Travel, and what breaks while you''re away\n\n**4. Re-check your Frankfurt connection.** Northbeam changed this flight on 17 Sep: **NB 412 LIS 10:25 → FRA 14:20**, then **NB 908 FRA 18:30 → HND 14:15+1** (was 17:55 → 13:40), seat 14C unchanged. That''s a 4h10m layover — comfortable, but confirm the booking reference **NB7Q4K** still matches and that no further change has landed since September.\n\n**5. Decide what happens to your recurring meetings, 9–13 Nov.** Your calendar does *not* know you''re travelling — it still has:\n- **Daily standup, 09:00 UTC** on Mon 9, Tue 10, Wed 11, Thu 12, Fri 13 → that''s **18:00 JST**, in the middle of your Tokyo evenings\n- **Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj, Tue 10 Nov 10:00 UTC** → 19:00 JST, from Tokyo\n\nYour \"Tokyo trip\" all-day block (Personal, 9–15 Nov) doesn''t block any of these. Either decline/skip the ones that don''t make sense or tell Raj the 1:1 is dial-in. Worth doing *this week* so nobody waits on you.\n\n**6. Try to see Kenji Watanabe while you''re there.** You''re in Tokyo 9–15 Nov and Aozora''s brand manager is in Japan. The remote packaging call already happened (15 Oct) and his 6 Sep email \"新ブランド案のご確認について\" is still sitting unanswered in your inbox. An in-person review of the packaging on the 20 Nov deadline beats another call.\n\n### P2 — Fix things that are quietly broken\n\n**7. Repair the \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" scheduled send.** It''s still **pending, scheduled for 5 January 2099**, addressed to yourself. The 5 Oct meeting notes action item was \"Ana sends the moodboard to Kenji on Friday\" — that never went out. Either send it properly or delete the broken schedule; right now it will sit there for 73 years.\n\n**8. Clear the stale read-later.** Your only read-later item is Brightloom order A-42 (\"Your order A-42 has shipped\", expected 30 Sep) — delivered weeks ago, nothing to action.\n\n### P3 — Workspace tidying, when you have a spare half hour\n\n**9. 278 unread emails, all the June-2024 \"Edge Sender\" test corpus.** Zero real unread mail. One bulk mark-as-read clears the badge.\n\n**10. Six duplicated drives + two with test junk.** They''re mirrors of the same Fernhill Studio drive; two S3 drives additionally carry an `edge/` fixture tree, and one FTP endpoint is scoped to `Clients/` only. Worth knowing before anyone assumes \"it''s in the drive\" means one canonical copy.\n\n---\n\n**What I''d actually do in the next 48 hours:** items 2 and 5 — get Tomás''s packaging proofs scheduled and sort out the 9–13 Nov meetings, because both get much harder once you''re in the air. Item 7 takes two minutes.\n\nWant me to:\n- **update the recurring 1:1 and standups** for 9–13 Nov (decline or add a note), or\n- **pull the Aozora packaging thread** so you can draft Tomás a concrete deadline?","createdAt":1793759689513}],"metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"},"content":"**Your week (Mon 2 – Sun 8 Nov 2026)** — the real drivers are a **Nov 9 flight to Tokyo** and an **Aozora delivery due Nov 20**, so this week is mostly prep, not meetings.\n\nFirst, housekeeping about the data: two of your four calendars are synthetic noise — **Bulk** has ~80 generated placeholder events (\"Bulk 169 package invoice draft\") and **Edge cases** has a \"Daily forever\" test event plus a ten-year all-day event. I''ve ignored both. Everything below comes from **Work** and **Personal**, plus mail and drive documents.\n\n### P0 — Critical path this week\n\n**1. Produce the Aozora rebrand final files — due Fri 20 Nov.** From `Clients/Aozora Ceramics/Rebrand/brief.md`: deliverables are wordmark + mark (three options at first review — done), colour and type system, and packaging for mugs, plates and gift box; budget JPY 1,850,000. You''re in Tokyo 9–15 Nov, so **you lose 7 of the 16 remaining days**. Decide this week what has to be finished and signed off *before* you fly.\n\n**2. Pin down the packaging art with Tomás before you leave.** The 5 Oct meeting notes have Tomás printing dielines and packaging tests using sea-green and chalk glazes, gift box first then mugs. The 8 mm / 0.25 pt minimum-stroke constraint is the acceptance test. This is the one piece that needs physical proofs — it can''t be rescued from a hotel room.\n\n**3. Book nothing for Fri 20 Nov.** That''s the delivery date and your first full week back.\n\n### P1 — Travel, and what breaks while you''re away\n\n**4. Re-check your Frankfurt connection.** Northbeam changed this flight on 17 Sep: **NB 412 LIS 10:25 → FRA 14:20**, then **NB 908 FRA 18:30 → HND 14:15+1** (was 17:55 → 13:40), seat 14C unchanged. That''s a 4h10m layover — comfortable, but confirm the booking reference **NB7Q4K** still matches and that no further change has landed since September.\n\n**5. Decide what happens to your recurring meetings, 9–13 Nov.** Your calendar does *not* know you''re travelling — it still has:\n- **Daily standup, 09:00 UTC** on Mon 9, Tue 10, Wed 11, Thu 12, Fri 13 → that''s **18:00 JST**, in the middle of your Tokyo evenings\n- **Weekly 1:1 Ana / Raj, Tue 10 Nov 10:00 UTC** → 19:00 JST, from Tokyo\n\nYour \"Tokyo trip\" all-day block (Personal, 9–15 Nov) doesn''t block any of these. Either decline/skip the ones that don''t make sense or tell Raj the 1:1 is dial-in. Worth doing *this week* so nobody waits on you.\n\n**6. Try to see Kenji Watanabe while you''re there.** You''re in Tokyo 9–15 Nov and Aozora''s brand manager is in Japan. The remote packaging call already happened (15 Oct) and his 6 Sep email \"新ブランド案のご確認について\" is still sitting unanswered in your inbox. An in-person review of the packaging on the 20 Nov deadline beats another call.\n\n### P2 — Fix things that are quietly broken\n\n**7. Repair the \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" scheduled send.** It''s still **pending, scheduled for 5 January 2099**, addressed to yourself. The 5 Oct meeting notes action item was \"Ana sends the moodboard to Kenji on Friday\" — that never went out. Either send it properly or delete the broken schedule; right now it will sit there for 73 years.\n\n**8. Clear the stale read-later.** Your only read-later item is Brightloom order A-42 (\"Your order A-42 has shipped\", expected 30 Sep) — delivered weeks ago, nothing to action.\n\n### P3 — Workspace tidying, when you have a spare half hour\n\n**9. 278 unread emails, all the June-2024 \"Edge Sender\" test corpus.** Zero real unread mail. One bulk mark-as-read clears the badge.\n\n**10. Six duplicated drives + two with test junk.** They''re mirrors of the same Fernhill Studio drive; two S3 drives additionally carry an `edge/` fixture tree, and one FTP endpoint is scoped to `Clients/` only. Worth knowing before anyone assumes \"it''s in the drive\" means one canonical copy.\n\n---\n\n**What I''d actually do in the next 48 hours:** items 2 and 5 — get Tomás''s packaging proofs scheduled and sort out the 9–13 Nov meetings, because both get much harder once you''re in the air. Item 7 takes two minutes.\n\nWant me to:\n- **update the recurring 1:1 and standups** for 9–13 Nov (decline or add a note), or\n- **pull the Aozora packaging thread** so you can draft Tomás a concrete deadline?"}','assistant','v2','2026-11-04T02:32:49.057Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('de199c46-5f66-429e-a1ba-4a231da20603','79652e77-d4f5-4c1b-93d1-e13d6f5393fb','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"text","text":"<turn sent-at=\"2026-11-04T02:34:49.531Z\" time-zone=\"UTC\" />","createdAt":1793759689539},{"type":"text","text":"Turn that to-do list into a short status update I could paste into chat.","createdAt":1793759689539}]}','user','v2','2026-11-04T02:34:49.577Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('0b24b4df-0b54-4fb8-a2d1-58e173deda9a','79652e77-d4f5-4c1b-93d1-e13d6f5393fb','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Write a short chat-ready status update. Plain text, pasteable, no markdown-heavy table. Keep it brief.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a short chat-ready status update. Plain text, pasteable, no markdown-heavy table. Keep it brief."}],"createdAt":1793759710929},{"type":"text","text":"Here''s a paste-ready version:\n\n---\n\n**Status — week of 2 Nov**\n\nTwo things drive this week: I fly to Tokyo Mon 9 Nov, and the Aozora rebrand final files are due Fri 20 Nov. So the week is mostly prep.\n\n**Critical path**\n- Aozora finals due 20 Nov — with the trip 9–15 Nov I lose 7 of the 16 remaining days. Need to lock what ships before I fly.\n- Packaging art with Tomás: gift box first, then mugs (sea-green + chalk glazes, 8mm min mark / 0.25pt stroke). This needs physical proofs, so it has to happen before I leave — not from Tokyo.\n- Fri 20 Nov is a hard delivery date; nothing else should land that week.\n\n**Travel**\n- LIS 10:25 → FRA 14:20, then FRA 18:30 → HND 14:15+1 (Northbeam NB7Q4K, seat 14C). Re-checking the connection — the FRA–HND leg was rescheduled on 17 Sep, 4h10m layover.\n- Want to see Kenji (Aozora) in person while I''m in Tokyo. His 6 Sep email on the new brand proposal is still unanswered, and an in-person packaging review suits the 20 Nov deadline better than another call.\n\n**Needs a decision**\n- My recurring standups (09:00 UTC, 9–13 Nov) and the 1:1 with Raj (Tue 10 Nov, 10:00 UTC) are still on the calendar — that''s 18:00–19:00 JST for me. Sorting those out this week so nobody''s waiting.\n\n**Cleanups queued**\n- \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" was scheduled by mistake for Jan 2099 and never went out — fixing.\n- 278 unread test emails from the June 2024 corpus (no real unread mail) — one bulk mark-as-read.\n- Six drives are duplicates of the same shared drive; two carry test folders. Nothing lost, just not canonical.\n\n**Next 48 hours:** get Tomás''s proof deadlines booked, sort the 9–13 Nov meetings.\n\n---\n\nHappy to tighten it further, or swap in specific dates/owners if this is going to someone who doesn''t have your calendar.","createdAt":1793759710929}],"content":"Here''s a paste-ready version:\n\n---\n\n**Status — week of 2 Nov**\n\nTwo things drive this week: I fly to Tokyo Mon 9 Nov, and the Aozora rebrand final files are due Fri 20 Nov. So the week is mostly prep.\n\n**Critical path**\n- Aozora finals due 20 Nov — with the trip 9–15 Nov I lose 7 of the 16 remaining days. Need to lock what ships before I fly.\n- Packaging art with Tomás: gift box first, then mugs (sea-green + chalk glazes, 8mm min mark / 0.25pt stroke). This needs physical proofs, so it has to happen before I leave — not from Tokyo.\n- Fri 20 Nov is a hard delivery date; nothing else should land that week.\n\n**Travel**\n- LIS 10:25 → FRA 14:20, then FRA 18:30 → HND 14:15+1 (Northbeam NB7Q4K, seat 14C). Re-checking the connection — the FRA–HND leg was rescheduled on 17 Sep, 4h10m layover.\n- Want to see Kenji (Aozora) in person while I''m in Tokyo. His 6 Sep email on the new brand proposal is still unanswered, and an in-person packaging review suits the 20 Nov deadline better than another call.\n\n**Needs a decision**\n- My recurring standups (09:00 UTC, 9–13 Nov) and the 1:1 with Raj (Tue 10 Nov, 10:00 UTC) are still on the calendar — that''s 18:00–19:00 JST for me. Sorting those out this week so nobody''s waiting.\n\n**Cleanups queued**\n- \"Moodboard for the rebrand\" was scheduled by mistake for Jan 2099 and never went out — fixing.\n- 278 unread test emails from the June 2024 corpus (no real unread mail) — one bulk mark-as-read.\n- Six drives are duplicates of the same shared drive; two carry test folders. Nothing lost, just not canonical.\n\n**Next 48 hours:** get Tomás''s proof deadlines booked, sort the 9–13 Nov meetings.\n\n---\n\nHappy to tighten it further, or swap in specific dates/owners if this is going to someone who doesn''t have your calendar.","metadata":{"modelId":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor","provider":"openai-compatible.chat"}}','assistant','v2','2026-11-04T02:35:10.929Z','f0c4be98-b2fd-59d7-b11e-c921e7d22615');
